{"duration_api_ms":34242,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"deef4f5d-3f8f-4f8b-9d06-dc4b54e81d08","total_cost_usd":2.544245,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308812,"cache_read_input_tokens":7565,"output_tokens":3611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1499},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308812,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":7565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":272515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3611,"cacheReadInputTokens":7565,"cacheCreationInputTokens":308812,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.544245,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1499,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the label to `labels/coder-1.json`. **The row codes rung 2, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\nIt has one row (`egi-draft-a1v2`) built on one record: AB 1955 (2023-2024). I coded two passages for it:\n\n| Passage | Class / kind | Shape | Key quote |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vote page (`33eca066…`) | `record` / `vote`, in-term, 2024-06-27 | `chair-shaped` | actor `Mike Fong, Muratsuchi, Ortega`; tally `Result: PASS, 61-16` |\n| Chaptered text (`c70fca3f…`) | `record` / `sponsor` (he is listed as coauthor) | `chair-shaped` | provision from Sec. 220.5(a): schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose…\" |\n\n**Why rung 2:**\n- **Not a preemption case.** Normally a law that stops another level of government from acting counts as off-dimension (rule H12). Here rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules, so the bill is on-question.\n- **Rung 1 is ruled out by the bill's own text.** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required to disclose.\" It never orders them to keep the information from parents, which is what rung 1 would need.\n- **Not near-unanimous.** 16 of 77 recorded votes were No, about 21%, so the vote can carry the chair.\n- **One subject.** The other parts of the bill (parent-support resources, anti-retaliation) cover the same pupil-rights matter, so I didn't treat it as a multi-subject bill.\n\n**Calls a reviewer may want to check:**\n- **Coauthor coded as `sponsor`.** Both passages are on the same bill, so code will count them as one source (`single-source`).\n- **When he joined as coauthor is uncertain.** This text was inserted by the Senate in May 2024, replacing the original bill. The coauthor line appears on the final chaptered version, so I took it as covering this text. The vote alone carries the chair either way.\n- **The disclosure ban has an exception:** \"unless otherwise required by state or federal law.\" I read it as not changing the rung.\n\n`needs_source` and `quotes` are empty: no source contains his own words.","ttft_ms":14209,"type":"result","duration_ms":37209,"uuid":"fb19234a-c665-4622-bc12-46aa64cd9b26","ttft_stream_ms":1135,"time_to_request_ms":475,"first_content_frame_ms":1135,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
